{"content":[{"c":["ANATHOTH (PLACE), ANATHOTHITE*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Town in Benjamin’s territory set aside for the Levites (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.18","r":"Josh.21.18","rawR":"Josh.21.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.18","value":"Josh.21.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 21:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.60","r":"1Chr.6.60","rawR":"1Chr.6.60","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.60","value":"1Chr.6.60"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:60"},"). Anathoth may have been named by the Canaanites for their goddess Anath, or later by the Israelites for one of Benjamin’s descendants (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.8","r":"1Chr.7.8","rawR":"1Chr.7.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.8","value":"1Chr.7.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:8"},"). The town was probably located at Ras el-Karrubeh near the modern town of Anata three miles (4.8 kilometers) north of Jerusalem. Its residents were sometimes called Anethothites or Anetothites (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.27","r":"2Sam.23.27","rawR":"2Sam.23.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.27","value":"2Sam.23.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.12","r":"1Chr.27.12","rawR":"1Chr.27.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.12","value":"1Chr.27.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:12"},"). Abiezer, one of David’s military leaders, was from Anathoth (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.28","r":"1Chr.11.28","rawR":"1Chr.11.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.28","value":"1Chr.11.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:28"},", KJV “Antothite”) as was the soldier Jehu (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.12.3","r":"1Chr.12.3","rawR":"1Chr.12.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.12.3","value":"1Chr.12.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 12:3"},") and the priest Abiathar (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.2.26","r":"1Kgs.2.26","rawR":"1Kgs.2.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.2.26","value":"1Kgs.2.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 2:26"},"). It was also the hometown of the prophet Jeremiah (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.1.1","r":"Jer.1.1","rawR":"Jer.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.1.1","value":"Jer.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 1:1"},"), though some of its inhabitants violently opposed him (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.11.21,23","r":"Jer.11.21,23","rawR":"Jer.11.21,23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.11.21,23","value":"Jer.11.21,23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 11:21, 23"},"). Just before Judah fell to Babylon, Jeremiah bought a field in Anathoth as a sign that Israel would be restored to her land (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.32.7-9","r":"Jer.32.7-9","rawR":"Jer.32.7-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.32.7-9","value":"Jer.32.7-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 32:7-9"},"). Years later, 128 men of Anathoth returned from the exile, and the town was resettled (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.32","r":"Neh.11.32","rawR":"Neh.11.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.32","value":"Neh.11.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:32"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AnathothPlaceAnathothite","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 21:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.18","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.18","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.18"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:60","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.60","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.60","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.60"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.8","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.7.8","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.7.8"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.27","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.27","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.23.27"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 27:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.27.12","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.27.12","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.27.12"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 11:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.28","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.28","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.28"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 12:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.12.3","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.12.3","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.12.3"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 2:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.2.26","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.2.26","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.2.26"},{"anchorText":"Jer 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.1.1","rawQueryValue":"Jer.1.1","sourceRefExact":"Jer.1.1"},{"anchorText":"Jer 11:21, 23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.11.21,23","rawQueryValue":"Jer.11.21,23","sourceRefExact":"Jer.11.21,23"},{"anchorText":"Jer 32:7-9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.32.7-9","rawQueryValue":"Jer.32.7-9","sourceRefExact":"Jer.32.7-9"},{"anchorText":"Neh 11:32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.32","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.32","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.32"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a7c97a61c4a758b9867765e5640c748aea6f9dca8bc6a27579399db19a0c003f","sourceItemName":"AnathothPlaceAnathothite","sourceItemOrder":340,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"AnathothPlaceAnathothite","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Anathoth (Place), Anathothite*","title":"Anathoth (Place), Anathothite*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}